    "evidence_text": "Experiments ::: Datasets\tWe construct three datasets based on IMDB reviews and Yelp reviews.\n\nWe filter out any review that has more than 400 tokens, producing the final dataset (imdb400).\n\nWe randomly partition both datasets into train/dev/test sets (90/5/5 for yelp50; 99/0.5/0.5 for yelp200).\n\nFor all datasets, we\n\nStatistics of the three datasets are presented in Table TABREF22.\n\nThese datasets present a variation in the text lengths (e.g. the average number of words for yelp50, yelp200 and imdb400 is 34, 82 and 195 words respectively), training data size (e.g. the number of training examples for target classifiers for imdb400, yelp50 and yelp200 are 18K, 407K and 2M, respectively) and input domain (e.g. restaurant vs. movie reviews).\n\nAll in all, the paraphrasability and fluency surveys suggest that imdb400 is an easier dataset for adversarial experiments, and it is the predominant dataset used by most studies.",
